{"v":1,"type":"session-summary","author_email":"contact@atkn.me","session":"kandev:83a0b430-49c1-4819-89d0-81c76deb6fd8","created_at":"2026-09-29T23:05:00Z","entries":[{"driving_event":"RVR-005 shipped the ledger with an authority field reserved and null and no way to say which remote is authoritative, so a repository with several publishing remotes had no principled answer and a fetched-but-unpromoted candidate had nowhere defined to go.","decision":"Give manifest.authority the primary remote name and keep the role vocabulary out of the manifest, resolving primary, mirror, archive, and import-only from reveries.remoteRole configuration; enforce quarantine in the write path by withholding the CAS on the identical validated candidate rather than by convention, parking it at the RVR-001 quarantine namespace; and verify mirrors by content against local remote-tracking refs, requiring a mirror to sign its own manifest bytes whenever the primary checkpoint is signed.","impact":"Absence of configuration stays benign: an unambiguous single publisher infers itself with no diagnostic and a repository declaring no roles keeps exact pre-existing behaviour, while conflicting, dangling, or non-publishing declarations are reported. A non-authoritative remote can be synced without ever being merged into the canonical notes ref, and a lagging mirror that is an ancestor is ordinary rather than a failure.","recurrence_control":"48 new tests across authority protocol, roles, mirror, import, and quarantine suites pin the three distinct predicates for sync promotion, publish destination, and sync source, the absent-versus-invalid distinction, and the quarantine withhold. Both schema-parity suites pass, which is the direct evidence that the manifest key set and the bytes signed in c370e81 did not move; the committed tree was verified in isolation at 491/491.","alternatives":["Require exactly one declared primary in every repository, which would report every existing multi-publisher repository as damaged and contradict the documented absent-is-benign rule.","Store the authority role inside the manifest so a checkpoint is self-describing, accepting that the signed bytes would then depend on configuration the manifest cannot see."],"sources":[{"relation":"implements","kind":"issue","ref":"github:phynics/reveries#17"}],"reveries":[],"retirements":[]}]}
